33,2,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,It seems we have a significant barrier for newcomers. Many are deterred by the lack of flexible entry points or the complexity of part-year fees.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It appears the administrative cost of ""flexibility"" is quite high. Chasing small payments is a recipe for treasurer burnout.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The data is quite stark. A small group is doing almost all the work and attending almost all the events, while others are virtually absent.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"It's not just about ""absent"" members. We've created a psychological barrier. People are weighing the cost of a weekday visit like it's a luxury purchase.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"The ledger is a disaster. Most of our money goes to fixed costs like hall hire. We can't afford to be ""flexible"" if the bank account is this thin.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, if we prioritize the bank account over accessibility, we will stop growing. We cannot let the fear of a thin margin kill the club's spirit.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"While I admire the spirit, Asuka, we must avoid a situation where the treasurer quits in a fit of exhaustion. Efficiency is a form of kindness.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"If we maintain a flat fee, we are essentially subsidizing the inactive members with the time and money of the active ones. That feels unsustainable.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Jonathan, a tiered system might just make the ""hesitant"" members feel even more like outsiders. We need to remove the friction, not add more categories.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, spirit doesn't pay the insurance. If we don't set a fee that covers the fixed costs upfront, we're just waiting for the club to collapse.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"A rigid, high upfront fee will only make the club feel like an exclusive club rather than a community. We need a way to let people drift in.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,Perhaps a simplified annual fee with a very limited number of exceptions? It would protect the treasurer's sanity and the club's solvency.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I wonder if a ""contribution"" model for those who use the facilities most would be better, or perhaps a discount for those who help with the rota.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"Let's be honest: the ""drift in"" approach is why the weekday turnout is pathetic. People don't commit because they don't feel they belong.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"I'm not interested in ""belonging"" if we can't pay the rent. We need a guaranteed sum from every member at the start of the year. No more guesswork.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, if we force a high entry price, we lose the very people who make the club worth running. We must find a way to keep it low-pressure.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,It seems we are caught between the desire for inclusivity and the reality of administrative exhaustion. A compromise is necessary.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I believe we should acknowledge the disparity. Those who carry the work should not be the ones paying the most for the privilege.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,I'll support whatever option actually encourages people to stop thinking and just show up. The current hesitation is a disease.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Takumi,,I'll support any option that ensures the fixed costs are covered without us having to beg for money in February.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
