59,3,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Option A is too rigid and will deter newcomers. Option C is a nightmare for the treasurer. Option B allows for a gradual entry into the community.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,Option C is an absolute non-starter. I've seen the hours spent chasing small sums; it is a recipe for misery. Option A is the most rational for the administrator.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,Option B seems the most equitable. It acknowledges that different members use the club differently and allows us to reward those who are more active.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Option C is exactly what killed the weekday turnout. Charging per event makes people ""weigh up"" the visit. Option A is the only way to restore a sense of ownership.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Takumi,,Option C is a joke. We'd be guessing our budget every single week. Option A is the only one that guarantees we can pay the hall hire.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, @Takumi, you are ignoring the newcomers. A high flat fee is a wall. Option B allows someone to start small and grow into the club.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shunichi"",""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, the ""wall"" of a flat fee is far less damaging than the ""wall"" of a treasurer who resigns because they've spent their weekends doing bookkeeping.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,But Option A ignores the fact that a few people are doing all the work. It feels wrong to charge the most active members the same as those who never show.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Jonathan, the ""privilege"" of being active is the activity itself. If you make it a transaction, you kill the culture. Option A makes the club a home, not a shop.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"Exactly. Option A is clean. You pay, you're in, the bills are paid. No chasing, no tiers, no guessing. It's the only way to be sure we're safe.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"If we choose Option A, we are essentially telling the people who are hesitant that they aren't welcome unless they commit a large sum upfront.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"I suspect the ""hesitant"" are more deterred by a lack of clear structure than by a single, transparent annual fee. Simplicity is often the most welcoming path.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I still struggle with the unfairness of it. However, if Option B is too complex to manage, I can see the appeal of Option A's stability.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Asuka, the hesitation comes from the lack of commitment. A flat fee creates a psychological contract. ""I've paid, so I should go."" It's basic psychology.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Takumi,,I'm not debating psychology. I'm debating the bank balance. Option A is the only one that ensures we don't end up in the red by mid-winter.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Asuka,,I cannot support a system that makes the club feel like an exclusive club. I will vote for Option B to preserve the possibility of a gentle entry.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"For the sake of the person who has to actually do the work, and for the stability of the club, I find Option A to be the only logical choice.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I value peace and fairness. While Option B is fairer, Option A provides the most peace for the committee. I will vote for Option B, hoping for fairness.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,I've made my case. We need to stop the hesitation and start the attendance. Option A is the only way to make the club feel like it belongs to the members.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Takumi,,I'm done with the guesswork. I'm voting for the only option that guarantees the bills are paid. Option A.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
